deep.reconstruction:
Setting. The notes study the 'structure at infinity' of the Deligne–Mumford stack M̄_{g,ν}. It is stratified by stable ('MD', i.e. Mumford–Deligne) graphs G, with stratum M_G and fundamental groupoid ΠM_G. A 'générisation' G→G' contracts a set of edges. M_{G,G'} is the germ (local branch) of the closure of M_{G'} along M_G. By (110)–(111) its fundamental groupoid is Π(M_G, Γ^!_{G,G'}), a twisted or covering version of ΠM_G determined by a subgroup Γ^!_{G,G'} of the automorphisms of G. ΠM*_{G,G'} is the 'punctured' version: the fundamental groupoid of the part of M_{G'} itself lying in a small neighbourhood of M_G along that branch. Homotopically this neighbourhood is a (Δ*)^{E}-bundle over the branch, where E is the set of contracted edges. So ΠM*_{G,G'} is an extension of ΠM_{G,G'} by Z^{E}, generated by Dehn twists around the vanishing cycles. There are maps γ_{G,G'}: ΠM*_{G,G'} → ΠM_{G'}.

This page. For a chain G→G'→G'' there is a canonical map ΠM_{G,G'} → ΠM_{G,G''}. It comes from the inclusion Γ^!_{G,G'} ⊂ Γ^!_{G,G''}, i.e. a map of germs of multiplicities M_{G,G'} → M_{G,G''}. Diagram (112) has three parts:
- the triple object ΠM*_{G,G',G''}, mapping by γ_{G,G',G''} to ΠM_{G''} (compatibility (91));
- ΠM*_{G,G'',} the punctured link of M_G inside M_{G''};
- the projections to ΠM_{G,G'} and to ΠM_{G,G''}.
Grothendieck asserts that the square
  ΠM*_{G,G',G''} → ΠM*_{G,G''}
  ↓              ↓
  ΠM_{G,G'} --can--> ΠM_{G,G''}
is 2-cartesian. ΠM*_{G,G',G''} was defined formally as an iterated 2-fibre product via (105), built from the two successive générisations. Concretely, it is the inverse-image (pull-back) of the extension ΠM*_{G,G''} → ΠM_{G,G''} along ΠM_{G,G'} → ΠM_{G,G''}. Geometrically: restrict the punctured tubular link of M_G in M̄_{G''} to the branch of M̄_{G'} through M_G.

Special case. Take G' to be the coarsest générisation (all edges contracted, the 'discrete' graph). Then S_AΠM_G := ΠM*_{G,G'} is defined; the next page continues this. It is an extension of ΠM_{G,G'} by Z^{A(G)} (A(G) = set of edges). Aut G acts on it, giving twisted local systems Z^{A(G)} on (ΠM_G, Γ') and quotients Z^C for Γ'-stable edge sets C. This is the fundamental-groupoid version of the punctured tubular neighbourhood of a boundary stratum. It is the gluing datum needed to reconstruct the homotopy type of M_{g,ν} from the strata, and serves the 'Lego'/Teichmüller-tower programme.
